# A `/static/*  /static/:splat  200` rule used to sit here, meant to stop the SPA
# fallback swallowing webpack's in-memory bundle during `netlify dev`. It could never
# have worked: a rewrite whose destination is its own source changes nothing, so the
# catch-all below still matched and served index.html as text/html where the browser
# expected JavaScript -- "Unexpected token '<'" and a blank page. Measured, not
# assumed: with the rule in place, /static/js/bundle.js returned 9246 bytes of HTML.
#
# It is gone rather than repaired, because it was compensating for a dev-server
# layering mistake rather than a redirect problem. We now browse CRA directly and
# forward only /.netlify/* to Netlify Dev -- see src/setupProxy.js. Netlify's redirect
# engine is no longer in the asset path, so there is nothing for it to swallow.
#
# Production never needed it: files there are on disk and are served before redirects
# are consulted, which is why beatflowmediagroup.com always returned real JavaScript.

# SPA fallback - must be last
/*  /index.html  200
